# Environment variables for wiki-server.
#
# systemd loads this via EnvironmentFile=-/etc/opt/wiki/wiki.env (the
# leading '-' makes the file optional — its absence does not stop the
# unit). The binary is installed under /opt/wiki, so FHS puts host
# config in /etc/opt/wiki/ — not /etc/sysconfig (RHEL SysV leftover)
# and not /etc/default (Debian packages that live in /usr).
# wiki-server itself does not read a hardcoded list of names; the one
# current consumer is CloudEmbeddingProvider, which getenv()s whatever
# NAME [embeddings].api_key_env points at in config.toml. Admin
# credentials still live in SQLite (wiki-server --create-admin); sessions
# are random opaque tokens, not signed by a secret from here.
#
# Copy to /etc/opt/wiki/wiki.env, chown wiki:wiki, chmod 600. Never put
# the key in config.toml — that file is plain text and sometimes ends up
# pasted into an issue or a screenshot.

# Name must match embeddings.api_key_env in config.toml (the example
# there uses this one). Leave unset / omit this line for a local
# OpenAI-compatible server that doesn't authenticate (Ollama, LM Studio).
# WIKI_EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY=
